Z||000004||Taijiguy||07-06-2000||10:58 AM||||You might feel a little silly when I tell you this, but I think you misunderstood when I said "not enough to worry about", I was making reference to the postage on the bolts I was offering to give you. Meaning the plenum/manifold bolt you were asking about. As for the vacuum lines, maybe this diagram will help:  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=964084&a=7062754&p=23874137&Sequence=0">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 07-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ironhorse||07-06-2000||11:08 AM||||before everybody start sending me pix of their emission hose routing pix. I already have that, and I follow it.  It' all works... my main concern is that stupid plenum as of where they go and where they hook up.  I CANNOT find any pix or information on it not even in hayes, the fiero bible, or that friggin pontiac dealer.  If someone please will.  open up their trunk/hood and trace their finger on where those hose go.  it 2 hose connecter on right side near the map sensor (not the map sensor itself) and where the hose connector on left side go to.    Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Taijiguy||07-06-2000||01:04 PM||||*sigh* no good deed goes unpunished....<P>OK, the two line connector you're talking about is attached to a manifold that runs along the front wall of the trunk space. The left side of the manifold is connected to the charcoal canister via rubber hose. The left side of the manifold also has two hoses (different sizes so as not to confuse them)with the connector. The mate to that connector has the two hoses running to the engine. One hose goes to that obscure vacuum connection I referred to in my first post, the other runs to the throttle body. That is actually pretty clearly represented in the diagram I attached. (You'll notice the two line connector in the drawing)<P>you're welcome.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ironhorse||07-06-2000||10:27 PM||||hey I'm sorry for the rough responds and such.  Sometime these things get to me and I go flyin off the handle. *sigh* I got them all except for one small vaccume line that's next to the map sensor.<P>Taijguy, about the bolt. yeah send them my way send me e mail kicker@choice.net and we'll talk.<P>Thanks for the help||||reg||1
